# Para VS Code REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP Client.
# Execute os logins, copie o accessToken obtido e substitua os tokens abaixo.
@baseUrl = https://localhost:8443
@userToken = COLE_TOKEN_USUARIO_AQUI
@adminToken = COLE_TOKEN_ADMIN_AQUI

### Login usuario (200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"usuario","password":"usuario123"}

### Login admin (200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"admin","password":"admin123"}

### Senha incorreta (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"usuario","password":"senha-incorreta"}

### Sem JWT (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos

### JWT invalido (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos
Authorization: Bearer token.invalido.aqui

### Pedido com usuario autenticado (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/pedidos
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Sem role ADMIN (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/status
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

### Com role ADMIN (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Acesso direto ao backend (403)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8081/internal/pedidos
X-Gateway-Authenticated: true

### OBS: o teste 429 deve repetir mais de 20 requisicoes em 1 minuto pelo mesmo IP.
### OBS: configure no cliente a confianca no certificado HTTPS autoassinado local.
